  "details": "I encountered a bug (on WINE/Linux, probably not your bug) where the semicylindrical HUD (mute/talking, etc.) is scrambled. CTRL+H does not hide it for me. I suspect that you are hiding the widgets on the HUD (making it full alpha) instead of removing it from the scene. It even covers the initial setup menu. I could work around this issue if (1) the HUD geometry was completely removed when hidden, and/or (2) a launch option was added to disable this particular HUD layer. All the other UI elements and rendering features I have encountered in the game work fine for me so far. (resubmitting request here per instructions)",
